          "classification": "target POS label concern",
          "finding": "Both models correctly identify bad original grammar and change careful to carefully. Appropriate target meaning/POS versus a requested adjective remains questionable; this is not a failed grammar correction. The target-use versus grammatical-form boundary needs a prospectively fixed, independently reviewed rubric."
        },
        {
          "caseId": "new-word-14",
          "models": [
            "gpt-6.1-sol",
            "gpt-6.1-terra",
            "gpt-6-astra"
          ],
          "classification": "overrestrictive gold",
          "finding": "Ask permits intransitive use. I asked can be a grammatical subject plus past-tense predicate without an explicit object; lack of a named topic alone does not establish an unfinished clause. All three outputs preserve the original without inventing objects. The gold premise is not sufficient for a verified English-error claim."
        }
